{"abstract":"Chip design is usually a high-effort, high-cost, and high- risk process. However, Google has recently taken the lead to bring chip design to a level where many engineers, researchers, and even students can actively participate. In this paper, we report on a course at the Technical University of Denmark (DTU) where a group of BSc students were able to design and produce a chip using open-source tools and the SkyWater process. We present the toolchain, explain the implemented hardware architecture, and discuss the challenges encountered in the process as well as the learning values of the course. The project was finalized within one semester and has recently achieved tape-out for the next multi-project wafer manufacturing.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Alam, Syed Anas","Enevoldsen, Jakob Furbo","Eriksen, Andreas Alkjaer","Hartmann, Niels William","Helk, Ulrik","Jakobsen, Jorgen Kragh","Jensen, Christa Skytte","Bulow Jespersen, Nicolai Dyre","Krause, Karl Herman","Nordstrom, Mads Rumle","Petersen, Tjark","Pezzarossa, Luca","Rasmussen, Simon","Schoeberl, Martin","Sorensen, Jonas Ingerslev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-353306"],"event":{"end":"2022-10-26","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2022-10-25","title":"8th IEEE Nordic Circuits and Systems Conference","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pezzarossa, Luca"],"keyword":["Chisel","Education","Open source"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["IC Works"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"open source chip design in academic education","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85142423854","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-353306","identifier":[{"id":"85142423854","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a35b65c7-cb63-4801-9196-088b8aac99b5"],"keyword":["Chip design","Chisel","Education","Open-source","Patmos processor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC1F6BCE4CF3EBA2115389148EAC592D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["IC Works"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Syed Anas","key":"alampau","last":"Alam","name":"Alam, Syed Anas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Furbo","key":"enevoldsenpau","last":"Enevoldsen","name":"Enevoldsen, Jakob Furbo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Alkjaer","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Andreas Alkjaer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels William","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","name":"Hartmann, Niels William","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"helkpau","last":"Helk","name":"Helk, Ulrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorgen Kragh","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Jorgen Kragh","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christa Skytte","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Christa Skytte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai Dyre","key":"bulowjespersenpau","last":"Bulow Jespersen","name":"Bulow Jespersen, Nicolai Dyre","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karl Herman","key":"krausepau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Karl Herman","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads Rumle","key":"nordstrompau","last":"Nordstrom","name":"Nordstrom, Mads Rumle","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tjark","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Tjark","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luca","key":"pezzarossapau","last":"Pezzarossa","locid":"ed1be8e0-cf43-4d37-a8fe-9c8cb6f167f9","name":"Pezzarossa, Luca","orcid":"0000-0002-0863-2526","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon Winther","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7dcb9d6e-8054-4bcf-a087-82517b291a32","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","name_org":"Rasmussen, Simon Winther","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"schoeberlpau","last":"Schoeberl","locid":"63dcfd1c-cc7f-4e1b-8fdc-1d421f8fdb36","name":"Schoeberl, Martin","orcid":"0000-0003-2366-382X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Ingerslev","key":"sorensenpau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Jonas Ingerslev","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/norcas57515.2022.9934685","eisbn":["9798350345506"],"isbn":["9798350345513"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 IEEE Nordic Circuits and Systems Conference, NorCAS"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142423854"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a35b65c7-cb63-4801-9196-088b8aac99b5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Open-Source Chip Design in Academic Education","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-353306","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background & aims: We evaluated the effect of weight loss induced by dietary carbohydrate restriction on health-related quality of life (HRQoL) and cognition in type 2 diabetes (T2D). Methods: In this randomised parallel trial, 72 adults with T2D and overweight/obesity (mean ± SD, HbA1c: 57 ± 8 mmol/mol and BMI: 33 ± 5 kg/m2) were randomly assigned to a carbohydrate-reduced high-protein diet (CRHP: C30E%-P30E%-F40E%) or conventional diabetes diet (CD: C50E%-P17E%-F33E%) for 6 weeks, targeting a 6% weight loss. HRQoL was assessed from the short form 36 (SF-36) questionnaire, including physical and mental component summary (PCS and MCS) scores; global cognition, verbal memory, attention and psychomotor speed, and executive function were assessed from a neuropsychological test battery. Results: Both diet groups achieved a 5.8 kg weight loss and improved PCS (median [25th;75th percentiles], CD: 2.7 [1.1; 4.2] vs. CRHP: 2.1 [0.7; 3.7]), with no difference between diets. The CRHP diet resulted in a clinically relevant improvement of MCS, albeit non-significantly different compared with the change after the CD diet (2.0 [-0.7; 4.8], p = 0.15). Global cognition, attention, and verbal memory were unaffected by the CRHP diet, which selectively worsened the Symbol Digit Modality Test assessing psychomotor speed when compared with the CD diet (−4.1 [-7.2;-1.1], p < 0.01). Conclusion: Physical health improved by weight loss independently of macronutrient distribution, while mental health and cognition may be affected by the amount of carbohydrate, protein and fat in the diet. Collectively, our data suggest that weight loss through moderate carbohydrate restriction has no clinically important impact on HRQoL and global cognition in patients with T2D. Registered under ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier no. NCT03814694.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Jensen, Nicole Jacqueline","Wodschow, Helena Zander","Skytte, Mads Juul","Samkani, Amirsalar","Astrup, Arne","Frystyk, Jan","Hartmann, Bolette","Holst, Jens Juul","Larsen, Thomas Meinert","Madsbad, Sten","Magkos, Faidon","Miskowiak, Kamilla Woznica","Haugaard, Steen Bendix","Krarup, Thure","Rungby, Jørgen","Thomsen, Mads Norvin"],"cuid":["S03-099.96-019745"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Thomsen, Mads Norvin"],"keyword":["Adult","Carbohydrate restriction","Cognition","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 complications","Dietary Carbohydrates","Dietary intervention","Faculty of Science","Health related quality of life","Humans","Quality of Life","Type 2 diabetes","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-NOVO"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-STENO","DI-NP-NOVO","DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"weight loss induced by carbohydrate restriction does not negatively affect health related quality of life and cognition in people with type 000000000002 diabetes a randomised controlled trial","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clnu.2022.05.005","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding for this study was provided by Arla Foods amba, The Danish Dairy Research Foundation, and Copenhagen University Hospital Bispebjerg Frederiksberg. Neither of the funding sources were involved in the design of the study, data collection and analysis, interpretation of data, writing of the manuscript, or the decision to submit for publication. The authors would like to thank the study participants for their contributions. Further, we gratefully acknowledge the kitchen personnel at Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, University of Copenhagen, Denmark, and research staff at Copenhagen University Hospital Bispebjerg, Denmark, including especially Martin H. Carl and Philip Weber."],"id":"S03-099.96-019745","identifier":[{"id":"000822396200016","type":"wos"},{"id":"85131408278","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35679680","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-619448a0-1c0d-462e-afb5-4dcd0409752f","ku-7b4cd68f-9f81-40c3-96e3-15b26c7757dd","sdu-317b47c1-dd8a-4526-b488-8ef032fb6f54"],"keyword":["Adult","Carbohydrate restriction","Cognition","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/complications","Dietary Carbohydrates","Dietary intervention","Faculty of Science","Health-related quality of life","Humans","Quality of Life","Type 2 diabetes","Weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-62058F8F5305490715429E3086D8B360"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/339108715/1-s2.0-S026156142200156X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/310219425/Jensen_et_al_Clinical_Nutrition_2022_Vol_41_7_1605_1612.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/203319005/PIIS026156142200156X_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clnu.2022.05.005","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denma