:"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hannah","key":"zuckermanhannahpau","last":"Zuckerman","name":"Zuckerman, Hannah","rank":1577,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ran","key":"lyuranpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Ran","rank":1578,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wayne","key":"pullanwaynepau","last":"Pullan","name":"Pullan, Wayne","rank":1579,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33326193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/database/baz085","issn":["17580463"],"journal":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","pages":"1-67","paperid":"085","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","title_org":"Database","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082592913"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88b053a3-63ab-4380-ab20-90a54b540224","au-6bf5b1c8-6cc1-4ee4-b711-48f478a90279","ku-291608f7-132f-41ac-94ae-fe9aa192baf0","sdu-a9479d7b-e13c-4f9b-8edd-dd71403513e8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Large expert-curated database for benchmarking document similarity detection in biomedical literature search","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-087.05-006608","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Resection of residual masses after chemotherapy plays a crucial role in management of patients with germ cell tumours (GCTs). The extent of surgery is controversial and we present the experiences from Aarhus University Hospital over a 20-year period. The aim was to evaluate survival, complications, working ability and quality of life (QOL) following a limited surgical procedure performed to resect residual masses in non-seminomatous testicular cancer patients after chemotherapy. MATERIAL AND METHODS: A consecutive patient cohort of 109 patients having surgery between 1993 and 2013 was investigated. Hospital records were reviewed and complications were graded according to the Clavien-Dindo classification. QOL data were assessed in a cross-sectional analysis using the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC), QLQ-C30 version 3.0. Patients were matched 1:1 with controls to evaluate the influence of surgical resection on the QOL. RESULTS: With a median follow-up of 10.3 years, 11 relapses in retroperitoneum were recorded in 10 patients (9%), and four patients (5%) died of disease progression. The majority of relapses in patients considered having no evidence of disease (NED) after primary retroperitoneal surgery occurred 10 + years after treatment and was outside the field of the elective lymph node dissection. Twenty-seven (44%) grade I, 15 (24%) grade II, 7 (11%) grade IIIa and 13 (21%) grade IIIb complications were recorded. No grade IV and V complications were observed. Twenty-three patients (20%) reported loss of antegrade ejaculation. We found no significant differences between patients and controls regarding QOL. CONCLUSION: The survival outcome and complication rate are favourable and are comparable to studies involving full and modified template lymph node dissection. We find that limited resection constitutes an applicable and safe procedure. Limited surgical resection did not influence the patients' long-term QOL. Longer follow-up might be considered.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schmidt, Anna Hartmann","Høyer, Morten","Jensen, Bent Frode Skov","Agerbæk, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-246206"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"limited post chemotherapy retroperitoneal resection of residual tumour in non seminomatous testicular cancer complications outcome and quality of life","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85044092888","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-246206","identifier":[{"id":"29537330","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044092888","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cc76d2b1-2500-429c-97d5-16eeceb2d7f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2657680E9B195237BC0E9E817AC0C55"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Hartmann","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Anna Hartmann","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"høyerpau","last":"Høyer","locid":"28b0c00c-755f-48a7-a13b-5efb6b9e1be6","name":"Høyer, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8609-0008","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bent Frode Skov","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Bent Frode Skov","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"agerbaekpau","last":"Agerbaek","locid":"d58a556e-d222-4312-b7b8-9e4f427fc3e5","name":"Agerbæk, Mads","name_org":"Agerbaek, Mads","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29537330"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2018.1449249","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"1084-1093","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044092888"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cc76d2b1-2500-429c-97d5-16eeceb2d7f1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Limited post-chemotherapy retroperitoneal resection of residual tumour in non-seminomatous testicular cancer: complications, outcome and quality of life","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-246206","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Glucagon is secreted from pancreatic α cells, and hypersecretion (hyperglucagonemia) contributes to diabetic hyperglycemia. Molecular heterogeneity in hyperglucagonemia is poorly investigated. By screening human plasma using high-resolution-proteomics, we identified several glucagon variants, among which proglucagon 1-61 (PG 1-61) appears to be the most abundant form. PG 1-61 is secreted in subjects with obesity, both before and after gastric bypass surgery, with protein and fat as the main drivers for secretion before surgery, but glucose after. Studies in hepatocytes and in β cells demonstrated that PG 1-61 dose-dependently increases levels of cAMP, through the glucagon receptor, and increases insulin secretion and protein levels of enzymes regulating glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis. In rats, PG 1-61 increases blood glucose and plasma insulin and decreases plasma levels of amino acids in vivo. We conclude that glucagon variants, such as PG 1-61, may contribute to glucose regulation by stimulating hepatic glucose production and insulin secretion.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J.","Kuhre, Rune E.","Hornburg, Daniel","Jensen, Christian Z.","Hornum, Mads","Dirksen, Carsten","Svane, Maria","Gasbjerg, Lærke S.","Jørgensen, Nils B.","Gabe, Maria N.","Balk-Møller, Emilie","Albrechtsen, Reidar","Winther-Sørensen, Marie","Galsgaard, Katrine D.","Meissner, Felix","Jorsal, Tina","Lund, Asger","Vilsbøll, Tina","Eliasen, Rasmus","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N.","Idorn, Thomas","Deacon, Carolyn F.","Knop, Filip K.","Rosenkilde, Mette M.","Hartmann, Bolette","Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","Mann, Matthias","Madsbad, Sten","Holst, Jens J"],"cuid":["S02-096.32-035421"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Alpha cells","GLP 1","Glucagon","L cells","Proglucagon","Proteomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating glucagon 000000000001 000000000061 regulates blood glucose by increasing insulin secretion and hepatic glucose production","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2017.10.034","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.32-035421","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5695911","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85034087701","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000414541700006","type":"wos"},{"id":"29117552","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-7b511021-3b07-43b6-9570-15b792cf700d","ku-5de0f9aa-7d95-4884-a486-1ef985f758da"],"keyword":["Alpha cells","GLP-1","Glucagon","L-cells","Proglucagon","Proteomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F42198E5AEEDBFFA70EFCDD4DFFD154A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2017.10.034","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/185994866/1_s2.0_S2211124717314663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139517968/1_s2.0_S2211124717314663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nord